#!/bin/sh
# claude-memento: Claude Code sessions wrapper for git-memento
# Translates "sessions get {id} --json" and "sessions list --json"
# into memento-compatible JSON by reading ~/.claude/projects/ directly.
#
# Usage:
#   git config memento.claude.bin "claude-memento"
#   git config memento.claude.getargs "sessions get {id} --json"
#   git config memento.claude.listargs "sessions list --json"

CLAUDE_PROJECTS="${CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR:-$HOME/.claude/projects}"

# --- sessions get {id} --json ---
cmd_get() {
  session_id="$1"
  jsonl=$(find "$CLAUDE_PROJECTS" -name "${session_id}.jsonl" 2>/dev/null | head -1)

  if [ -z "$jsonl" ]; then
    echo "Session '${session_id}' not found in ${CLAUDE_PROJECTS}" >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  # Extract title and convert JSONL messages to memento format in a single pass
  python3 - "$jsonl" "$session_id" <<'PYEOF'
import sys, json

jsonl_path = sys.argv[1]
session_id = sys.argv[2]

title = None
messages = []
with open(jsonl_path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
    for line in f:
        line = line.strip()
        if not line:
            continue
        try:
            obj = json.loads(line)
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            continue

        msg_type = obj.get("type", "")
        if msg_type not in ("user", "assistant"):
            continue

        message = obj.get("message", {})
        role    = message.get("role", msg_type)
        content = message.get("content", "")

        # content can be a string or list of content blocks
        if isinstance(content, list):
            parts = []
            for block in content:
                if isinstance(block, dict):
                    parts.append(block.get("text", ""))
                elif isinstance(block, str):
                    parts.append(block)
            content = "\n".join(p for p in parts if p)

        if not isinstance(content, str):
            content = str(content)

        if content.strip():
            # Extract title from first user message
            if title is None and role == "user":
                title = content.strip()[:80].replace("\n", " ")
            messages.append({"role": role, "content": content})

result = {
    "id":       session_id,
    "title":    title,
    "messages": messages
}
print(json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False))
PYEOF
}

# --- sessions list --json ---
cmd_list() {
  python3 - "$CLAUDE_PROJECTS" <<'PYEOF'
import sys, json, os, glob

projects_dir = sys.argv[1]
sessions = []
seen = set()

for jsonl_path in glob.glob(os.path.join(projects_dir, "**", "*.jsonl"), recursive=True):
    session_id = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(jsonl_path))[0]
    if session_id in seen:
        continue
    seen.add(session_id)

    title = None
    try:
        with open(jsonl_path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            for line in f:
                line = line.strip()
                if not line:
                    continue
                try:
                    obj = json.loads(line)
                except json.JSONDecodeError:
                    continue
                if obj.get("type") == "user":
                    msg     = obj.get("message", {})
                    content = msg.get("content", "")
                    if isinstance(content, list):
                        content = " ".join(
                            c.get("text", "") for c in content if isinstance(c, dict)
                        )
                    if isinstance(content, str) and content.strip():
                        title = content.strip()[:80].replace("\n", " ")
                        break
    except Exception:
        pass

    sessions.append({"id": session_id, "title": title})

print(json.dumps(sessions, ensure_ascii=False))
PYEOF
}

# --- argument dispatcher ---
# Expected call patterns:
#   claude-memento sessions get <id> --json
#   claude-memento sessions list --json
case "$1/$2" in
  sessions/get)
    cmd_get "$3"
    ;;
  sessions/list)
    cmd_list
    ;;
  *)
    echo "claude-memento: unknown command: $*" >&2
    echo "Usage: claude-memento sessions {get <id> --json | list --json}" >&2
    exit 1
    ;;
esac
